// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-059
=adr: 059
=title: Alarm Notification Channels + Escalation Policies
=date: 2026-04-17
=status: accepted

#ctx
~AlarmInstance ISA-18.2 state machine fires alarms but has no outbound delivery mechanism
~No escalation path when ACTIVE_UNACKED alarms age past operator response threshold
~Notification model (ADR task) already exists for workflow:sendNotification — in-app only
~HeartbeatService (ADR-041) and WorkflowSchedulerService (ADR-040) establish node-cron singleton pattern

#opts
=opt_A: Push all notifications synchronously from alarm creation — blocks ingest path
=opt_B: Fire-and-forget from alarm creation + separate escalation cron — non-blocking, consistent with ADR-020/041
~selected: opt_B

#decision
~NotificationChannel model (orgId, name, type:email|webhook|in-app, config:{to,smtpHost}|{url,headers}|{})
~EscalationPolicy model (orgId, alarmRuleId?:ObjectId optional, tiers:[{delayMinutes,channelIds[],minimumSeverity}])
~AlarmNotificationService: sendToChannel(channel, alarm) — nodemailer(email) | fetch(webhook) | Socket.io(in-app) — fire-and-forget, errors logged only
~AlarmService.createInstance(): after ISA-18.2 insert, call AlarmNotificationService.notifyOnCreate() fire-and-forget (same pattern as dispatchDeviceStateChange in ADR-020)
~AlarmEscalationService: node-cron 60s singleton — query ACTIVE_UNACKED where createdAt < now−tier.delayMinutes; match EscalationPolicy by alarmRuleId (exact) then orgId wildcard; dispatch via AlarmNotificationService; idempotent (track dispatched tiers in AlarmInstance.escalatedTiers[])
~AlarmInstance gains escalatedTiers:number[] field (tier indices already dispatched — prevents re-fire)
~Routes: /notification-channels (CRUD, Admin+) | /escalation-policies (CRUD, Admin+)
~SMTP env: SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_FROM added to config.ts + .env.example
~Wire AlarmEscalationService in index.ts after HeartbeatService (same SIGINT/SIGTERM teardown)

#consequences
=breaking: AlarmInstance gains optional escalatedTiers field — existing docs unaffected (undefined treated as [])
=perf: +1 compound query per 60s poll (index: orgId + state + createdAt); +nodemailer dep
=email: SMTP_HOST unset → email channels skip silently (stub mode, no crash)
=webhook: native fetch with 10s AbortController timeout (same pattern as executeActionCallWebhook)
=scope: frontend = new /alarm-management page (NotificationChannels tab + EscalationPolicies tab)

#scope
=arch_summary_update: yes
=extends_adrs: [ADR-020, ADR-041, ADR-040]
=new_models: [NotificationChannel, EscalationPolicy]
=modified_models: [AlarmInstance (+escalatedTiers)]
